    "justification_quote": "The counterexample relies on the premise that fine-tuning a foundation model constitutes 'task-specific optimization.' The literal assertion states that the platform 'lacks task-specific optimization,' which describes an inherent capability or design feature of the platform role, not merely the absence of post-training adjustments. The counterexample's factual premise—that LoRA fine-tuning achieves high performance—is true in isolation but does not refute the claim about the *platform's* lack of built-in optimization. The logical gap exists because optimizing a model via external techniques (fine-tuning) is distinct from the platform possessing intrinsic task-specific optimization mechanisms.",
