  },
  "refutes_exact_assertion": {
    "conclusion_quote": "Consequently, the case fails to establish that the assertion is false.",
    "justification_quote": "The counterexample does not successfully refute the literal assertion because it conflates 'external fine-tuning' with 'intrinsic task-specific optimization.' The assertion claims the platform lacks the latter; the case provides evidence of the former. Since a different method (fine-tuning) does not refute the existence or lack of a specific internal feature (optimization), the objection is invalid. The premise that fine-tuning equals optimization in this context is unsupported by the strict reading of 'task-specific optimization' as an inherent platform property.",
